   "evidence": "Mathlib `Function.Injective.comp_left (hg : Injective g) : Injective (g \u2218 \u00b7)` (Mathlib/Logic/Function/Basic.lean:233) uses `left` for the left factor of `\u2218`; `Injective.of_comp_right ... (hg : Surjective g)` for `f \u2218 g` (line 213) uses `right` for the inner map.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Logic/Function/Extend.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to `Function.extend_comp_of_injective_left`, and update the module-docstring entry (line 31) and the use in `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/ExtendByZero.lean` `linearMap_comp`.",
   "issue": "`extend_comp_of_injective_right` says the right factor is injective, but the hypothesis is `Injective f\u2082\u2083`, which is the left factor of `f\u2082\u2083 \u2218 f\u2081\u2082`. The right factor `f\u2081\u2082` is the one the lemma allows to be arbitrary, so the name points users at the wrong map.",
   "line": 96
  }
